export anchor NewswireStyle:
    number: 398
    screen: EmailClient
    name: Newswire
    idea: The inbox reads as a wire service feed on a perforated dark paper strip, with every message filed under a timestamp, a priority code and an uppercase slug, and the open message set as wire copy.
    base: dark
    palette:
        room: #121316, the page, the desks column and buttons
        strip: #1c1d21, the feed paper and the style sheet
        strip2: #23252a, the item on screen
        perf: #0a0b0d, the sprocket holes
        rule: #3a3c43, dashed and double rules
        type: #ecebe6, text, the ticker band and the primary button
        grey: #a9a8a2, slugs, ledes and labels
        flash: #ff6d5e, the NEW priority block and the WIRE tag
        onFlash: #1d0400, text on flash
        highlight: #f5d547, the current desk, the STARRED box and focus
        onHighlight: #1d1800, text on highlight
    type:
        A mono stack, IBM Plex Mono, SF Mono, ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas,
        at a 14px base for slug lines, copy and labels. Headlines use a
        gothic stack, Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial, with the masthead 30px caps, the story headline 38px at 700
        and feed headlines 20px, bold when unread. The copy is 16px at 1.75.
        Slug lines are 12px caps.
    layout:
        A cream ticker band runs across the top with a red WIRE tag and the
        three newest items in one line. A masthead reads Brightwork Mail
        Wire over a double rule, with Desk of Mara Okafor, morning file and
        an underlined search led by a slash. Three columns follow. The
        left, DESKS, lists the folders in caps with Inbox 12 on a yellow
        bar led by a caret, then BEATS for the labels. The middle is the
        feed on a slightly lighter strip with a column of round sprocket
        holes down its left edge. Each item has a slug line with the time
        in bold, a priority code, an uppercase slug such as NORTHPASS-DEMO
        and the beat, then the headline as sender and subject, then an
        optional lede led by a dash. Items are split by dashed rules. The
        open item is shaded, ruled in yellow and marked ON SCREEN. The
        right column is the story, a slugbar, the big headline, FROM, TO
        and FILED pairs, the copy behind a grey left rule, an end mark of
        dashes around 30, and a joined strip of buttons each with its key,
        Reply in cream. Below 1100px the story drops under the feed. On a
        phone the feed comes first, then the story, then the desks.
    spacing: A 4px base. 10 to 12px item padding, 20 to 24px column padding, a 44px left gutter for the sprocket strip.
    density: High. Three columns of text with a slug line above every headline.
    corners: Square. Nothing is rounded but the sprocket holes.
    borders: 1px dashed rules between items, 3px double rules under the masthead and above the sheet, a 2px solid rule over the story.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Typographic only. A filled square plus NEW in a red block, an
        asterisk plus STARRED in a yellow box, plus one ATTACHED, a caret on
        the current desk, and an end mark under the copy.
    focus: A 2px yellow outline offset 2px.
    tone: Wire desk shorthand in capitals, such as DESKS, BEATS, FILED, ROUTINE and YDAY.
